sequenceDiagram
    participant C1 as Client (Tab 1 - pay 80k)
    participant C2 as Client (Tab 2 - pay 90k)
    participant PS as Payment Service
    participant US as User Service
    participant DB as User DB (balance = 100k)

    par Request 1 arrives first
        C1->>PS: POST /transactions (amount=80000)
        PS->>US: deduct balance (userId, 80000)
        US->>DB: findOneAndUpdate({_id, balance >= 80000}, {$inc: {balance: -80000}})
        Note over DB: Single atomic operation on one document.<br/>MongoDB serializes writes to the same document,<br/>Request 2 is applied after this one.
        DB-->>US: balance = 20000
        US-->>PS: 200 OK (new balance = 20000)
        PS-->>C1: 201 Created - OTP sent (status otp_sent)
    and Request 2 arrives almost same time
        C2->>PS: POST /transactions (amount=90000)
        PS->>US: deduct balance (userId, 90000)
        US->>DB: findOneAndUpdate({_id, balance >= 90000}, {$inc: {balance: -90000}})
        Note over DB: Runs after Request 1: balance is now 20000,<br/>filter balance >= 90000 matches no document
        DB-->>US: null
        US-->>PS: 409 Conflict - insufficient balance
        PS->>PS: release the reserved fee (compensating transaction)
        PS-->>C2: 402 Payment Required - "Số dư không đủ"
    end

    Note over C1,DB: Result: only Request 1 succeeds.<br/>Final balance = 20000 (correct, never negative)
